Algorithm:

Step 1: Initialize low = 0 and high = m.
Step 2: Perform Binary Search while low <= high.
Step 3: Find mid = (low + high) / 2.
Step 4: Initialize num = 1 (long type) to store mid^n.
Step 5: Run a loop n times and multiply num = num * mid to compute mid^n.
Step 6: If num == m, return mid because mid is the nth root.
Step 7: If num > m, move left by setting high = mid - 1.
Step 8: If num < m, move right by setting low = mid + 1.
Step 9: Repeat the process until the search space ends.
Step 10: If no integer nth root is found, return -1.

Time Complexity: O(n × log m)
Space Complexity: O(1)


-----> Code <-----

class Solution {
    public int nthRoot(int n, int m) {
        // code here
        int low=0;
        int high=m;
        while(low<=high){
            int mid=(low+high)/2;
            long num = 1;
            for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
                num = num * mid;
            }
            if(num==m){
                return mid;
            }
            else if(num>m){
                high=mid-1;
            }
            else{
                low=mid+1;
            }
        }
        return -1;
        
    }
}
